claimed: intent-slot-descriptor — request 5 of the consumer seven, the last one still open, and they said propose it rather than wait for them. The Overview promises that a label cannot be acted on and a filled FRAME can, and no type currently holds a frame: Temporal parses one slot in one language and nothing describes what a slot IS. Their shape, which they arrived at from having built one: a slot is a NAME, a question to ask when it is unanswered (per language), and a parser String => Option[Value] whose failure is a RE-ASK rather than a silently stored string. Under that description Temporal is one parser among several, another language is another parser rather than a rewrite, and the CRF lane becomes an alternative implementation of the same seam instead of a separate design. Propose the type, send it for review, and keep the classifier a pure function of a message -- the slot descriptor describes, it does not converse.
